WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.936
-Our guests tonight
are three of

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:04.503
my favorite people
in the world.

00:00:04.503 --> 00:00:07.507
Please welcome back
to our annual Thanksgiving show

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:10.543
my family -- Hillary,
Larry and Josh Meyers.

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:15.214
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.214 --> 00:00:22.922 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:30.630 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:38.337 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:38.337 --> 00:00:42.108
Welcome back, everybody.
The Meyers family.

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:43.743
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:46.245
Now, this is very
exciting because last year,

00:00:46.245 --> 00:00:49.115
obviously COVID was
in a far worse place

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:51.217
and we basically decided
a few days out

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:52.551
we would all stay at home.

00:00:52.551 --> 00:00:54.053
You guys were in New Hampshire,
two different rooms.

00:00:54.053 --> 00:00:55.388
Josh, you were in L.A.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:57.490
It's very nice
to be here in person.

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.058
I think they think two different
rooms is where --

00:00:59.058 --> 00:01:00.960
You are sometimes
in the same room.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.930
-Yes.
-It goes better when you're not.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.731
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.731 --> 00:01:08.434
And, Josh, the scariest thing
that happened

00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:10.703
was we were we were in Zooming

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:13.506
and you decided to do
your interview from the bathtub.

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:16.075
-Yeah, I decided --
Well, I was in my house

00:01:16.075 --> 00:01:17.509
and I was like,
change of venue,

00:01:17.509 --> 00:01:20.013
change of location
for the second act or third act,

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:21.414
whatever you want to call.
Yeah.

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:24.717
-And then while you were
Zooming in a bathtub, you froze.

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:26.452
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:01:26.452 --> 00:01:32.425
-And there was a fear
amongst all of us here

00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:34.060
that you had electrocuted
yourself in the bathroom.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:36.563
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, which is a valid fear.

00:01:36.563 --> 00:01:39.131
You know I've got
a lighting kit set up

00:01:39.131 --> 00:01:40.633
and I've got a computer.

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:43.236
-A lot of things tipping on
the side of a bathtub ledge.

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:44.304
-Yeah.

00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:45.805
-Was it scary for you
in the moment?

00:01:45.805 --> 00:01:48.107
-No, just the lights went out.
-Yeah.

00:01:48.107 --> 00:01:50.376
-The lights went out
and I didn't know

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:53.713
if it was just, like,
my Internet or my apartment,

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:56.983
and I didn't want to
get out of the tub

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:58.918
because my bubbles were gone.
-Right.

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:00.086
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:02.621
-In case the power
kicked back on...

00:02:02.621 --> 00:02:04.591
-Right, at an inopportune
moment.

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:06.959
-Right.
-Not only is this show canceled,

00:02:06.959 --> 00:02:08.494
but you personally
are canceled.

00:02:08.494 --> 00:02:09.728
[ Laughter ]
-Or not.

00:02:09.728 --> 00:02:11.898
It's weird.
It's weird who gets canceled

00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:14.066
and who doesn't these days.
-I think the bummer is you were

00:02:14.066 --> 00:02:15.602
in the middle of a story
when you got frozen.

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:18.103
So let's just show that clip.
-Sure.

00:02:18.103 --> 00:02:19.472
-And then just pick it up

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:21.140
right when it gets frozen
and finish the story for us.

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:23.309
-Okay, yeah.
I get on the couch.

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:26.145
I would get a warm blanket
wrapped around me.

00:02:26.145 --> 00:02:30.516
I'd be given a bagel with cream
cheese and bacon and juice.

00:02:30.516 --> 00:02:33.620
And I would watch
"The Smurfs" and "The Snorks."

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:35.855
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:38.624
Yeah, every every morning
I was woken up.

00:02:38.624 --> 00:02:40.159
And she would have drawn
a bath for me,

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:43.395
and that's how my love
of baths was created.

00:02:43.395 --> 00:02:45.231
-So, I feel
like having a full 12 months

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:47.032
between the middle
and the end of the story

00:02:47.032 --> 00:02:49.635
probably hurt it a little.
-Probably a little bit, yeah.

00:02:49.635 --> 00:02:52.605
-We also talked last year
about how the next time

00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:55.674
you were going to see our boys,
my boys,

00:02:55.674 --> 00:02:57.076
that you were going to dress up

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:59.679
like the White Rabbit
from "Alice in Wonderland."

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:03.416
And I had my doubts
that you would do that.

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:05.385
-That's disappointing to hear.
-Yeah.

00:03:05.385 --> 00:03:07.086
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:11.523
Well, no one was disappointed
on the day.

00:03:11.523 --> 00:03:15.261
Take a look. I should --
If you like cute videos,

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:16.762
there's going
to be a fair share today.

00:03:16.762 --> 00:03:17.931
Take a look at this one.

00:03:19.698 --> 00:03:21.067
-Panka Yarry's late.

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:23.803
-I'm late for
a very important date!

00:03:23.803 --> 00:03:25.838
No time to say "Hello", goodbye!

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:27.540
I'm late! I'm late!
I'm late! I'm late!

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:31.044
I'm overdue!
I'm in a rabbit stew!

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:33.045
No time to say "Hello," goodbye!

00:03:33.045 --> 00:03:35.714
I'm late, I'm late, I'm late,
I'm late, I'm late!

00:03:35.714 --> 00:03:38.117
I'm late for
a very important date!

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:40.453
No time to say "Hello," goodbye!
I'm late, I'm late, I'm late!

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:42.922
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:46.525
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:46.525 --> 00:03:49.195
-Now...

00:03:49.195 --> 00:03:51.931
Over the course
of this past year,

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:53.832
you're not a man
who rests on your laurels.

00:03:53.832 --> 00:03:57.403
So, you knock out White Rabbit.

00:03:57.403 --> 00:03:59.738
Then the kids get into Babar.

00:03:59.738 --> 00:04:01.841
He shows up.
[ Audience aws ]

00:04:01.841 --> 00:04:03.843
And then the Flash.

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:06.946
The Flash showed up.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.946 --> 00:04:09.415
[ Applause ]

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:14.219
-And you wouldn't believe
how crazy fast he was.

00:04:14.219 --> 00:04:16.088
-Oh, my God, this is --
Yeah, it doesn't look it.

00:04:16.088 --> 00:04:18.925
But this is exactly as fast as
the fastest Flash.

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:20.426
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:22.228
-Ain't no Flash like a Flash
with a stache.

00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:23.396
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:25.064
-Ain't no Flash like a Flash
with a stache.

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:29.135
Now, we have another because --
You explain how it first --

00:04:29.135 --> 00:04:30.503
Do you remember
how it first started,

00:04:30.503 --> 00:04:33.005
what Dad decides to do
as he pulled into the driveway?

00:04:33.005 --> 00:04:34.707
-Oh, the honking business?
-Yes.

00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:38.310
-Yes, well, I think it was
Pittsburgh had that honk --

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:39.645
bum, bum, bum-bum-bum.

00:04:39.645 --> 00:04:40.947
-When we were in high school,

00:04:40.947 --> 00:04:43.849
when we would pull up
to our friends

00:04:43.849 --> 00:04:45.784
to let them know
we were out there,

00:04:45.784 --> 00:04:47.720
we would always honk
a certain way.

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:49.254
There were some
high school fraternities

00:04:49.254 --> 00:04:50.556
and we called it a Pi Tau.

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:52.992
And we used to go
dah, dah, dah-dah-dah,

00:04:52.992 --> 00:04:54.026
and then you would always know

00:04:54.026 --> 00:04:55.461
it was
one of your friends for you.

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:58.097
-Well, now my kids know.

00:04:58.097 --> 00:05:00.233
They get so excited
when they hear it.

00:05:00.233 --> 00:05:03.503
And this is a series
over the course of the last year

00:05:03.503 --> 00:05:05.971
of my boys hearing the honk.

00:05:05.971 --> 00:05:08.641
And I should note,
the last part of this clip

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:10.609
is you guys leaving.

00:05:10.609 --> 00:05:12.177
And it's a slightly
different reaction.

00:05:12.177 --> 00:05:15.447
Also, I forgot to preface,
for those who don't know this,

00:05:15.447 --> 00:05:20.119
my kids call my parents
Panka Yarry and Panka Hurry.

00:05:20.119 --> 00:05:23.155
Panka was how my oldest son
said grandpa, and it stuck.

00:05:23.155 --> 00:05:25.424
So take a look at the Pankas
arriving.

00:05:25.424 --> 00:05:32.532
[ Horn honking rhythmically,
kids laughing ]

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:38.637
[ Horn honking rhythmically ]

00:05:38.637 --> 00:05:41.307
-[ Laughing ]

00:05:41.307 --> 00:05:44.776
-Ah! Aaah! Aaah!

00:05:44.776 --> 00:05:47.446
[ Honking continues ]

00:05:47.446 --> 00:05:48.881
[ Laughter ]

00:05:59.892 --> 00:06:03.129
[ Laughter ]

00:06:03.129 --> 00:06:08.100
[ Kids screaming ]

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:09.535
[ Laughter ]

00:06:11.103 --> 00:06:14.373
[ Laughter ]

00:06:14.373 --> 00:06:16.876
-Hi! Hi!

00:06:16.876 --> 00:06:18.544
That's the Flash, by the way.

00:06:18.544 --> 00:06:20.646
[ Laughter ]

00:06:20.646 --> 00:06:22.648
-Say bye, guys.

00:06:22.648 --> 00:06:25.351
-Bye!
-Bye!

00:06:25.351 --> 00:06:27.520
[ Audience aws ]
-[ Cries ]

00:06:30.022 --> 00:06:32.291
[ Laughter ]

00:06:32.291 --> 00:06:33.992
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:33.992 --> 00:06:36.162
-They seem to be fans.

00:06:39.097 --> 00:06:41.133
They seem to be fans.

00:06:41.133 --> 00:06:43.969
We want everybody
to stick around

00:06:43.969 --> 00:06:45.705
because up next,
we have,

00:06:45.705 --> 00:06:48.473
I guess, I think you can call it
a surprise announcement,

00:06:48.473 --> 00:06:50.776
which I think will be
very fun for everybody.

00:06:50.776 --> 00:06:53.045
We'll be right back with more
Hillary, Larry, Josh

00:06:53.045 --> 00:06:55.081
and a surprise
Meyers family announcement.

